      <div type="clause" n="74.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 74.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 74.3" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="591" ed="#liebermann"/>Si alicuius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Hn_74-3.lnote.oe.35"/> homo ex contencione aliqua uel rebus repentinis occidatur, requirat eum dominus suus per plegium et pro mortuo plenam et eam rectitudinem offerat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="p" target="#Hn_74-3.lnote.oe.p"/>, quam pro uiuo faceret, de quo rectum non difforciauerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Hn_74-3.lnote.oe.36"/>.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 591 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_74-3.lnote.oe.p" n="p" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">591</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">anders</hi> 70, 10. 83, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">differently 70, 10. 83, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_74-3.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">591</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aliquis <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aliquis Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_74-3.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">591</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">defo. <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">defo. Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_74-3.lnote.oe._" n="-" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Vassallität 20; Grab 3a. 4—75 am Rande spät: <hi rend="italic">Hominem dominum suum nequiter occidentem quasi</hi> [?] <hi rend="italic">incomparabiliter puniendum, eo quod celus huiusmodi ceteris criminibus detestabilius reputatur</hi> Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Vassallität 20; Grab 3a. 4—75 in the margin, in a late hand: <hi rend="italic">Hominem dominum suum nequiter occidentem quasi</hi> [?] <hi rend="italic">incomparabiliter puniendum, eo quod celus huiusmodi ceteris criminibus detestabilius reputatur</hi> Rs</seg></note>
